wikitext.en:Union of Radical Republicans:
{{other uses|Radical Party (France)}}
The '''Union of Radical Republicans''' (''Union des républicains radicaux'', U2R) is a [[list of political parties in France|French political party]] with its origins in the Radical faction of the [[Pôle républicain|Republican Pole]], an organization rallying together supporters of [[Jean-Pierre Chevènement]]'s candidacy for the [[2002 French presidential election|2002 presidential election]]. It included members of the [[Left Radical Party]],  including [[Emile Zuccarelli]], as well as [[Republican, Radical and Radical-Socialist Party|''Valoisien'' Radicals]], including [[Gérard Benhamou]], a former [[Union for French Democracy|UDF]] MEP.

The U2R has since distanced itself from Chevènement's [[Citizen and Republican Movement]] (MRC), and supported [[François Bayrou]]'s candidacy for the [[2007 French presidential election|2007 presidential election]]. However it later distanced itself from Bayrou and joined [[The Progressives]].

